course: dictionary
lesson: 12604
title: Disconnection: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Disconnection is a noun, and it can mean cutting something off, a break in a link, or a feeling of not being close to others. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «The power company made a disconnection because the bill was not paid.» The words power company and bill tell you that a supply was cut off.
explain: Here is a science sentence. «There was a disconnection in the circuit, so the bulb did not glow.» A circuit needs every part joined up. The clue is the broken link: when the link breaks, electricity cannot flow, so the bulb stays dark.
explain: The third meaning is about feelings, not things. «After she moved to a new town, Maya felt a sense of disconnection from her old friends.» No wire was cut here. A sense of disconnection means she no longer felt close to people she used to know. Ask yourself: is this about a thing or a feeling? That tells you which meaning to pick.
fact: Disconnection is a noun: one disconnection, many disconnections.
fact: Disconnection can mean cutting off a supply, such as electricity, gas, water, phone or internet.
fact: Disconnection can also mean a break in a link between things, such as in a circuit.
fact: Disconnection can mean a feeling of not being close to, or in touch with, other people or things.
fact: Phrases to know: «disconnection from», «face disconnection», «a sense of disconnection».
exercise: «The power company made a disconnection because the bill was not paid.» What does disconnection mean here? | A bright new light for the street | A big party with music | *A cut-off of a supply, such as electricity | A happy meeting of two families
exercise: «There was a disconnection in the circuit, so the bulb did not glow.» What does disconnection mean here? | A bright colour on the wall | A loud noise from the kitchen | *A break in a link between parts | A friendly chat
exercise: «After she moved away, Maya felt a sense of disconnection from her old friends.» What does sense of disconnection suggest? | *A feeling of not being close to people | A plan to visit her friends every day | A feeling of being very hungry | A map of the new town
test: «Families who cannot pay their bills may face disconnection of their water.» What does face disconnection mean? | *Have their water cut off | Get free water every day | Hear a loud noise from the pipes
test: Which of these is an example of disconnection in computing? | *The internet stopping for a whole afternoon | A game with new levels | A broken laptop screen | A website full of pictures
exam: Which sentence uses disconnection to mean a feeling? | *Ben felt a disconnection from his cousins after they moved abroad | The wire was joined back together | The lights went off in the cellar | Water came out of the tap
